          "Engage affluent homeowners on fiscal governance and quality of life: at $105K income with 45.8% college education, this constituency evaluates on whether government is competent, whether schools are well-funded, whether infrastructure is maintained, and whether healthcare policy is rational — not on abstract conservative positioning or cultural appeals.",
          "Do not concede the renter and working-class constituency: the 34.4% renter rate and 17.4% Hispanic population represent real people with real economic concerns around housing affordability, wage stagnation, and access to healthcare — if Democrats are winning these voters decisively, it is because they are offering concrete answers to those concerns that Republicans are not."
