          { name: "Assuming Minority Communities Are Unpersuadable or Immobile", tag: "avoid", why: "The presence of 8.06% Hispanic, 5.32% Black, and 4.63% Asian residents in a $143,204-income district suggests college-educated, economically mobile minority households whose political preferences are not predetermined — they may respond to messaging about inclusive opportunity, healthcare costs, and economic mobility that neither major party is currently offering them in this specific market. Any candidate who writes off these communities as either safely Democratic or inevitably Republican is abdicating the actual work of constituent engagement that competitive elections require." }
