          "Lead with housing affordability and economic mobility in suburban context: renters in expensive Maryland suburbs face real housing-cost pressure despite the district's $143,204 median income, and this is the most direct economic concern for a renter and younger-adult constituency that may not respond to abstract partisan positioning.",
