          "Defend actively on education investment and school funding: the 40.4% college-educated population is concentrated in professional households with school-age children for whom public education quality is a primary governance concern. Republican candidates who cannot articulate a substantive education agenda beyond tax rhetoric will lose persuadable suburban families to Democratic opposition.",
          "Engage the 40.4 median-age professional constituency on economic security concerns: housing affordability, healthcare costs, and student loan burdens affect affluent young professionals differently than they affect older homeowners. Democratic messaging on these issues resonates with college-educated younger adults, and Republican candidates must offer concrete alternatives rather than abstract conservatism.",
          "Maintain high constituent service and local visibility: in an affluent, educated district where partisan margins are soft, candidates who are visible, responsive, and engaged in local governance build personal political capital that inoculates against partisan swings. Unopposed victories breed complacency; sustained constituent engagement is the actual defense against future Democratic challenges."
