          { name: "Generic Democratic Messaging Without District-Specific Economic Content", tag: "avoid", why: "A $95,984 median income, college-educated, majority-renter district in an urban area is not evaluating on abstract partisan or cultural positioning—it is evaluating on whether state government is addressing housing costs, student debt, healthcare access, and economic opportunity. The 29% result suggests the 2024 campaign relied on generic Democratic messaging without connecting to these constituencies' material concerns. Any campaign that repeats this pattern—leading with party identity rather than concrete policy answers to housing, healthcare, and economic mobility—will fail to recover the 40+ points necessary to compete in this district." }
