          "Rebuild organizational infrastructure in a college-educated, urban constituency with the networks and resources to sustain serious field operations: volunteer recruitment, voter contact, and digital engagement at a scale that the 2024 result suggests was absent. A $95,984 median income district with 50.9% college education can support sophisticated campaign operations if the candidate and campaign are credible.",
          "Lead with economic messaging that speaks directly to this district's material concerns: housing affordability and development in an urban area with 50.6% renters, student loan policy and career pathway concerns for college-educated young professionals, healthcare access and costs, and whether state policy is delivering economic opportunity for the next generation. Abstract partisan rhetoric will not recover from 29%.",
