          "Segment by life stage, not just demographics: the 38.7 median age and 33% renter rate mean the constituency includes younger professionals, middle-aged homeowners with school-age children, and approaching-retirement professionals with distinct material priorities — each requires specific messaging on career mobility, education quality, healthcare costs, or tax sustainability rather than undifferentiated professional-class appeal.",
          "Treat the 100% Democratic sweep as an opportunity, not a lock: unopposed status does not indicate unshakeable partisan dominance in an affluent, educated, professional community — it indicates the absence of organized opposition. A well-resourced challenger with credible fiscal and governance positioning can contest this seat; an incumbent should assume 2026 will be competitive and build a record of specific material delivery.",
