          "Sustain minority community turnout, especially among Hispanic/Latino and Black constituents, by demonstrating specific legislative wins on economic mobility, workforce development, healthcare equity, and criminal justice—at 27.8% Hispanic and 14.6% Black, these communities represent the swing margin that determines whether Democrats hold all three seats or lose one to a Republican challenger.",
          "Address the renter and younger-adult constituency's material concerns directly: the 35.8% renter rate and 39.8 median age signal housing costs, childcare, and student debt as primary economic pressures; legislative agenda that includes rent stabilization, childcare subsidies, and student loan relief will activate this constituency and suppress Republican persuasion in 2026.",
          "Do not treat the 100% 2024 result as a durable baseline: in a three-seat at-large race, the third-place finisher may have won with significantly fewer votes than first and second place, creating a vulnerable seat if Republican turnout or candidate quality improves, or if Democratic turnout declines from 2024's presidential-election levels."
