          "Treat the unopposed 2024 result as a warning, not a victory lap: the absence of organized opposition reflects no challenger's focus on this district, not voter satisfaction with the incumbent; any credible candidate who offers concrete solutions to aging-homeowner economic concerns can rapidly become competitive.",
          "Engage the 17.9% renter minority as a secondary but growing constituency: younger renters and aging renters on fixed incomes both face housing affordability constraints in an affluent district, and specific policy solutions on rental market regulation and senior affordable housing can build a coalition beyond the homeowner base.",
          "Monitor property tax trends and healthcare cost data obsessively: these are the two issues most likely to generate either incumbent vulnerability or challenger opportunity in an affluent, aging district where constituent satisfaction is primarily determined by whether material costs are rising or falling."
