          "Engage the high-renter constituency (46.8%) on affordability and transit: younger professionals and urban-oriented residents prioritize housing costs, public transportation, and walkable neighborhoods; Democratic advantage here is real, but only if state policy actively supports affordable housing and transit investment rather than allowing them to become luxury commodities.",
          "Monitor for Republican apertures on governance delivery: in a high-income, educated district, swing voters evaluate on whether government works, not ideology; any perception that Democratic governance is generating service failures, cost overruns, or inefficiency creates an opening for a credible Republican challenger to argue for management competence over partisan identity."
