          "Lead with housing affordability and renter protection as governance priorities: at 52.3% renters with 66.1% college education and $90,173 income, this is a constituency for whom rent-to-income ratio, tenant rights, housing discrimination enforcement, and development policy are material economic concerns, not abstract platform positions.",
