          "Lead with upper-middle-class governance: education funding and public school quality, property tax management, small-business support, and infrastructure investment in a district where the median household income and college attainment place economic concerns above the state average.",
          "Consolidate the Black-majority base (50.66%) by demonstrating specific engagement with economic mobility, healthcare access, and wealth-building in Black communities—not ceremonial acknowledgment, but measurable policy and constituent service outcomes that show the representative is actively serving this demographic majority.",
          "In a two-seat at-large race, recognize that the absence of Republican opposition in 2024 does not guarantee future contestation will not emerge; build a constituent relationship architecture that is durable across the full demographic spectrum rather than assuming the 100% margin is a permanent floor."
