          { name: "Ignoring the Renter Majority's Distinction from Homeowner Constituencies", tag: "avoid", why: "Policy and rhetoric that works for homeowner-majority districts — property tax policy, school funding tied to home values, neighborhood stability framed through real estate — does not address the material concerns of a 47.2% renter constituency with median income of $55,428. Candidates who rely on homeowner-oriented framing or fail to distinguish between renter and owner economic interests are not speaking to how a plurality of the district actually lives and what they need from government." }
