          { name: "Generic Democratic Coalition Building Without Community-Specific Service Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "MD-47A is heavily Democratic, which means that the real political competition is among Democrats and community stakeholders competing for resources and representation—not between Democrats and Republicans. A candidate who campaigns as a generic Democrat without specific commitments to the Black community's distinct priorities (criminal justice, healthcare equity, community investment) or to the Hispanic community's distinct priorities (immigration enforcement, workplace protection, language access) is leaving both communities vulnerable to a challenger who promises more specific service delivery. The absence of Republican opposition in 2024 means that the competitive space shifted entirely to which candidates best represent community interests within a Democratic framework; ignoring that shift and running a generic Democratic campaign is strategically obsolete in this district." }
