          "Address education funding and school quality directly; a 40.4% college-educated, $116,549-income district with homeowners has direct material interest in public school performance and will evaluate candidates partly on education policy credibility.",
          "Recognize that the 35% Democratic opposition in an affluent suburban district likely concentrates among college-educated professionals and younger affluent households—do not assume the margin is stable if Democratic messaging on healthcare, education, or environmental protection resonates more credibly than Republican alternatives."
