          "Avoid treating 73% as permission to neglect constituent service or assume intraparty dominance is permanent; in a district this educated and civically engaged, word-of-mouth about governance failures spreads quickly, and a primary challenger with credible focus on school equity or infrastructure could credibly compete despite the Democratic lean."
