          "Engage each demographic constituency on material interests, not as a unified 'base': the 36% white, 27% Hispanic/Latino, 18% Black, and 12% Asian communities have distinct economic concerns and governance expectations around housing, education funding, public safety, and economic mobility — treating them as separate constituencies with specific policy attention prevents the perception that any group is being taken for granted.",
