          "Recognize that 99% is not a mandate to govern without accountability—it is a supermajority that must be continuously earned through demonstrated constituent responsiveness on the material issues that drive voting behavior; any primary challenger who demonstrates superior engagement on housing, healthcare, or economic opportunity can shift the flow of that overwhelming Democratic support."
